#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Terminator Line: the dusk offensive on Tarn, 2311.  A sample game for
the Grognard engine, and an original one.

Tarn is an airless moon that turns once in thirty days, so the line
between its day and its night crawls across the ground at a walking
pace.  The Concord's landing force comes down on the night side and
attacks west behind the dusk, toward the mass driver at Sable Port that
throws the Free Holds' ore into orbit.  Whatever stands in the sunlight
is seen for miles, and easy to hit.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./terminator (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.terminator.json.  ./terminator --selftest checks the map
and plays a game between two computer players.
"""

